  "limits": [
    "Five owned 64 MiB snapshot virtio fixtures and one boot-image disk; actual UFS root on 14.5 and ZFS root on 15.1. No physical/controller/multipath/shared-host qualification.",
    "Actual direct read-only, alias read-only and alias read/write descriptors held only on independently verified HVM-UNIQUE-512. No bytes written through those handles; all five guest disk hashes match before/after, root mount/GUID/backing preserved, handles close before existing filesystem fixtures begin.",
    "Native provider/consumer aggregate access agrees while actual handles are held. Opening direct/alias handles invalidates prior review, independently recollected unchanged held access validates, closing restores zero counts and invalidates the held-open review. Unsupported actual mode controls modify capture copies only.",
    "Counts include consumers and alias propagation, are not exact process/descriptor counts or PID attribution. Native exclusive counters are observed aggregate semantics, not a userspace O_EXCL enforcement guarantee or a product lock.",
    "All previous fixture/system/imported/exported/signature assertions rerun: 68 assertions in the same four tests. All original host backings/base/runtime preserved, owned disks/image/key/variables removed and supervisor groups stopped. Previous immutable manifest hashes retain their original sources.",
    "Zero aggregate counts are not full signature/partition absence, exported-pool absence, locality, remote-host inactivity, enrollment, reservation or complete device clearance. Local inspection cannot fence a competing root actor.",
    "Unknown/error/incomplete/contradictory captures refuse a zero observation. Syntax cannot establish successful execution, freshness, completeness, provenance or atomicity. No runtime collector/helper/HTTP/CLI wiring, transport/persisted schema, submitted jobs or product writes.",
    "M2-DEVICE-001, complete slice 1 and later M2 acceptance gates remain open. Final PR-head portable review is separate; documentation/evidence updates must leave all functional/test/tool input hashes unchanged."
  ]
